  "readmeFile": "README.nuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.5.0: targets .NET 10 (and netstandard2.0). Anti-triggers (negative context): a number next to invoice, order, article code, protocol... is no longer read as a phone number (UseNegativeContext, AddNegativeKeywords, negative_keywords, global_negative_keywords). Wider detection: printed IBAN, IP addresses (CIDR, ranges), URLs, monetary amounts, dates of birth, document protocol numbers, dotted card numbers, landlines starting with 0, more phone keywords. Fixed the Italian VAT checksum. 1.4.0: optional ML confirmation tier - IMlEntityDetector / PrivacyAnalyzer.MlDetector / MlSpan (the learned PrivacyGuardML model ships in the CavemanML package); a failed checksum still vetoes. 1.3.1: False-positive hardening ported from Synthelion 1.2.5 - a failed checksum is never detected or masked, bare numeric formats are gated by requires_context + nearby keyword, short keywords match as whole words, Maltese ID tightened, spaced phone/card numbers. 1.3.0: Streaming & document masking (ported from Synthelion 1.2.5 privacy_stream.py / document_extractor.py). PrivacyStreamMasker: boundary-safe chunked/streaming PII masking with a configurable overlap window (default 512 chars) so patterns spanning a chunk boundary are caught; Feed()/Flush() API for incremental streams and a MaskStream() convenience helper for chunked iterables. PrivacySession.Summary(): redacted placeholder+category view (never the original value) safe to log/display/return over APIs, unlike GetAll()/ToJson() which carry cleartext PII (their XML docs now warn about this). DocumentMasker: streaming masking of plain text, Markdown and CSV files into a \"name.masked.ext\" copy next to the source (the original is never overwritten) — files are processed in chunks, never loaded whole; CSV rows are read with a minimal RFC-4180-aware reader so quoted multi-line cells survive. Added 12 new regression tests. 1.2.2: NuGet icon restored (caveman-icon.png now packed and referenced via PackageIcon).",
